# tools/ holds project-local toolchain binaries that we vendor rather
# than rely on the developer's PATH for. Per PROP-000 §16, JTD codegen
# lives here. The binaries themselves are NOT committed — each
# subdirectory carries a README.md pinning the upstream version and
# install procedure. New machines run the install command from the
# README to populate this directory.
#
# Top-level `.sh`, `.ps1` and `.py` scripts ARE committed — vendored helper
# scripts (e.g. `self-check.sh`) live here and are part of the source
# tree, not generated tooling output. Python joined that list when a
# corpus-wide migration needed a committed, re-runnable inverse: a script
# that can undo a rewrite is worthless if it is not in the history beside
# the rewrite. It does not belong in a campaign zone — those are disposable
# by design, and this project has already paid for filing durable things
# there.
*
!.gitignore
!*/
!*/README.md
!*.sh
!*.ps1
!*.py
# The progress dashboard (campaign plan §7) is committed source, not a
# vendored binary: zero-dependency node:http server + one static page.
!progress-dashboard/serve.mjs
!progress-dashboard/index.html
